The function is already a minimal inline wrapper around the base-class generic setter, so any direct manipulation would require private members and risk behavioral changes. I kept the exact call, which the compiler inlines to the same optimal code.

```cpp
    void SetTimestamp(FIT_DATE_TIME timestamp)
    {
        SetFieldUINT32Value(253, timestamp, 0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```